WEBVTT

00:37.500 --> 00:40.289
- A-Team roll call. Face?
- Here and handsome.

00:40.380 --> 00:43.003
- Murdock?
- Here, and crazy!

00:43.093 --> 00:45.086
- BA?
- I pity the fool.

00:45.179 --> 00:48.265
But I also suggest ways
he may better himself.

00:48.351 --> 00:53.645
This is gonna be a fun day. Much better than
that day I tried TAG body spray for sick cats.

00:57.949 --> 01:00.406
Oh. Oh. Oh, God. Oh, God.

01:02.373 --> 01:04.497
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

01:08.048 --> 01:12.797
You're cute. You're cute.
I don't wanna pet you, though.

01:12.890 --> 01:14.968
Oh, all right.

01:16.562 --> 01:19.434
What are you gonna do?
What are you gonna do?

01:19.525 --> 01:22.694
Oh! Oh, no! OK, no.
Yeah, no, this spray is not for me.

01:25.577 --> 01:28.698
- Brian, what are you doing here?
- You lookjust like ALF.

01:28.789 --> 01:31.828
<i>I'm not ALF.
I'm Douglas Brackman from L.A. Law.</i>

01:31.919 --> 01:34.460
<i>I'm writing an article
for the Daily Shopper.</i>

01:34.548 --> 01:37.717
You'll have a lot to write
after we win the costume contest.

01:37.804 --> 01:40.047
Hey, check it out. Bill Cosby aerobics.

01:46.277 --> 01:50.026
OK, everyone, Alan Thicke will be up
in a minute to answer your hate mail,

01:50.115 --> 01:56.240
but first, the winners of this year's costume
contest, the A-Team with the real black guy.

01:58.086 --> 02:02.716
OK, you can stop with that cigar now, Gary.
My sinuses will thank you.

02:10.939 --> 02:14.525
<i>Brian, I read your article in the Daily Shopper.
It was wonderful.</i>

02:14.613 --> 02:17.402
- Don't oversell it, Lois.
- No, it was good.

02:17.493 --> 02:20.199
It almost felt like it was written
by a real writer.

02:20.289 --> 02:24.074
I read your article too. You should spend
less time working for the paper

02:24.169 --> 02:28.750
and more time working
on that novel you've been working on.

02:28.843 --> 02:29.876
Brian.

02:29.971 --> 02:33.306
<i>This is Wellesley Shepherdson
calling from The New Yorker.</i>

02:33.392 --> 02:38.140
- Perhaps you've heard of us?
- Yeah, of course I've heard of you.

02:38.233 --> 02:42.482
<i>I was using the Daily Shopper to shoo away
a homeless person and I saw your article.</i>

02:42.572 --> 02:46.491
We'd love to talk to you about
becoming a contributor. Come by tomorrow.

02:46.581 --> 02:48.490
Wow, yeah, that'd be great.

02:48.583 --> 02:51.955
<i>Two o'clock. They want me
to contribute to The New Yorker.</i>

02:52.048 --> 02:55.832
<i>The New Yorker? You'll fit in there
as well as I did at Woodstock.</i>

02:55.928 --> 03:01.518
Excuse me, it's been brought to my attention
that a few bad apples are smoking marijuana.

03:01.604 --> 03:04.808
I've got news for you, my friend.
Marijuana's illegal.

03:04.900 --> 03:06.810
Not cool. All right, then.

03:14.081 --> 03:15.874
- You suck!
- Learn the rules!

03:18.047 --> 03:21.381
Our writers' lounge,
where you'll meet some contributors.

03:21.468 --> 03:23.628
- Fielding Wellingtonsworth.
- Hello.

03:23.722 --> 03:25.931
- Livingston Winstofford.
- Yes.

03:26.017 --> 03:29.139
- Amelia Bedford-Furthington-Chesterhill.
- Good day.

03:29.231 --> 03:31.984
And James William Bottomtooth.

03:33.029 --> 03:36.863
- This is Brian, our newest contributor.
- Hi, there. How's it going?

03:36.952 --> 03:38.910
- Would you like some tea?
- Cigar?

03:38.996 --> 03:41.488
Brandy?

03:41.584 --> 03:44.671
- No, I'm good, thanks.
- We read your article, Brian.

03:44.756 --> 03:49.171
Your study in postmodern American
subcultures was quite illuminating.

03:49.263 --> 03:52.052
Wow, thanks.
That means a lot coming from you guys.

03:55.481 --> 03:57.558
I'm sorry?

04:00.447 --> 04:02.524
Yes?

04:06.207 --> 04:10.040
- Is there a bathroom around here?
- Yes, yes, follow me.

04:12.007 --> 04:16.054
<i>- Where are the toilets?
- No one at The New Yorker has an anus.</i>

04:18.977 --> 04:23.855
Peter, it's been two weeks. Don't you think
it's time to take off your A-Team costume?

04:23.943 --> 04:29.023
Yeah, I guess so, but part of me wished we
could just be the A-Team forever, you know?

04:29.118 --> 04:32.820
Oh, this damn chair keeps wobbling.
I think one of the legs is short.

04:32.915 --> 04:37.996
- Lance, I told you to fix that chair.
- I checked it earlier. It seems fine.

04:39.384 --> 04:42.755
That chair's always like that. We'll help you.

04:46.979 --> 04:48.095
Wow, thanks.

04:48.190 --> 04:53.733
Hey, if we could fix that wobbly chair, think
of what else we could do for our community.

04:53.823 --> 04:59.331
Cleveland's right. It seems it's our destiny
to be the A-Team after all.

04:59.415 --> 05:01.540
We're the A-Team, yeah!

05:02.086 --> 05:08.092
In 2005, a group of local misfits won
a costume contest at an '80s TV convention.

05:08.179 --> 05:11.598
These men promptly returned home
and drank some beer.

05:11.685 --> 05:14.143
Today they survive as soldiers of fortune.

05:14.231 --> 05:18.396
If you have a problem, if no one else can help,
and if you can find them,

05:18.487 --> 05:20.945
maybe you can hire the A-Team.

05:59.010 --> 06:04.685
<i>So I said to him, "Brown liquor before
Labor Day? What, do you work for Esquire?"</i>

06:04.768 --> 06:08.222
Oh, Brian, how droll.
We'll have to put that into a cartoon,

06:08.317 --> 06:11.153
or as we call it,
an illustrated laughing square.

06:11.237 --> 06:14.775
You went to Harvard? I'm an Ivy-League man
myself. I went to Brown.

06:14.869 --> 06:19.700
My incarcerated business partner's retarded
gay niece went to Brown. What year?

06:19.794 --> 06:22.202
Well, I mean, I didn't technically graduate.

06:22.297 --> 06:24.790
You're a college dropout?

06:24.885 --> 06:29.514
<i>Brian, The New Yorker does not employ
your kind. You, sir, are fired.</i>

06:43.414 --> 06:48.708
I can't believe they fired you. How come you
never told us you dropped out of college?

06:48.798 --> 06:51.373
<i>I saw an Afterschool Special about that.</i>

06:51.469 --> 06:56.180
It didn't work out too well for Kristy
McNichol, but then again, nothing did.

06:56.268 --> 07:00.599
I was only one course shy of graduating
and I just cracked under the pressure.

07:00.692 --> 07:03.064
Now itjust cost me the bestjob I ever had.

07:03.153 --> 07:06.607
Don't take it too hard.
You're not the first person to get fired.

07:06.700 --> 07:10.867
Louis, the French people really
wanna thank you for your services as king,

07:10.958 --> 07:17.130
but, it's just not working out
and we've decided to go another way, so...

07:17.218 --> 07:18.629
Yeah.

07:18.720 --> 07:22.138
I just heard the dog got fired.
Did I miss it? Did he cry yet?

07:22.226 --> 07:25.431
Oh, come on, dog. cry for me.
Ah, there you are.

07:25.523 --> 07:29.308
Oh, yeah, cry for Stewie.
Life isn't what you thought it would be.

07:29.403 --> 07:32.739
Boy, not graduating from college
has haunted me for years.

07:32.826 --> 07:36.778
Well, if you only had one class left
why don't you just go back and finish?

07:36.873 --> 07:40.162
- Plenty of people do that.
- You know, that's not a bad idea.

07:40.255 --> 07:44.337
Well, this is boring.
Let's go see what Meg is up to.

07:51.272 --> 07:53.349
Hello, Meg...

08:16.937 --> 08:19.264
- What are you doing here?
- Are you kidding?

08:19.357 --> 08:23.489
Miss watching you crash and burn in
this misguided attempt to finish college?

08:23.573 --> 08:26.859
You're not staying. I'll call Lois
and have her pick you up.

08:26.952 --> 08:30.324
Hi, I'm your roommate Caleb.
I like cutting myself.

08:30.417 --> 08:33.254
I bleed a lot. Can I have the top bunk?

08:33.339 --> 08:37.588
He already has a roommate - me.
We're a couple of crazy college kooks.

08:37.679 --> 08:40.967
We're about to make a hilarious
answering-machine message.

08:41.060 --> 08:44.395
You've reached Stewie and Brian.
We're not here right now.

08:44.481 --> 08:47.687
If this is Mom, send money
because we're college students

08:47.778 --> 08:50.400
and we need money
for books and highlighters

08:50.490 --> 08:56.912
and ramen noodles and condoms
for sexual relations with our classmates.

08:59.630 --> 09:02.550
All right, fine, you can stay,
but what do I tell Lois?

09:02.636 --> 09:05.923
You don't have to tell her.
Gary Coleman owed me a favour.

09:06.016 --> 09:10.514
- Stewie, you want more strained peas?
- What you talkin' 'bout, vile woman?

09:12.567 --> 09:14.478
There she is, boys, all done.

09:14.570 --> 09:18.784
The A-Team is ready to help rid the world
of injustice and evil.

09:19.411 --> 09:21.371
Yeah!

09:21.457 --> 09:23.747
- All right!
- Yeah!

09:37.232 --> 09:39.558
Let's do it!

09:47.790 --> 09:50.365
This is advanced physics, right?

09:50.462 --> 09:52.704
I have a right to defend myself as a woman!

09:52.798 --> 09:55.837
- No means no!
- What the hell is wrong with you?

09:55.929 --> 10:00.225
I'm sorry. I just came from that
orientation seminar about college dating.

10:00.310 --> 10:04.143
Hi, I'm Kelly McGillis,
and I'm here to talk to you about rape.

10:04.232 --> 10:07.152
Ladies, look to your left.
Now look to your right.

10:07.237 --> 10:11.569
Statistics indicate
that both of those men will rape you.

10:11.661 --> 10:13.952
- I'm not gonna rape you.
- I might.

10:15.083 --> 10:18.501
- Good morning, class.
- Can I borrow a pencil?

10:18.589 --> 10:23.930
- Now, now, it looks like we have a comedian.
- I wasn't making ajoke, I was just asking...

10:24.014 --> 10:28.227
Now, Louie Anderson, our first test is Friday,

10:28.312 --> 10:32.016
and if you don't pass you are out of the class.

10:33.947 --> 10:36.486
Fluffy! Fluffy, come down!

10:36.576 --> 10:39.115
Oh, Mommy, Daddy, what are we gonna do?

10:41.959 --> 10:47.835
Don't you worry, sad little girl. The A-Team'll
get your beloved kitty down. Ready, boys?

11:00.697 --> 11:04.696
- No need to thank us, it's what we do.
- Who the hell are you guys?

11:06.206 --> 11:08.699
We're the A-Team.

11:13.968 --> 11:18.432
- Get off my property!
- Yeah, that's probably a good idea. Let's go.

11:22.774 --> 11:25.444
What do you think?
I got this at the school store.

11:25.528 --> 11:30.028
<i>It's an MC Escher drawing.
I think it's called Crazy Stairs.</i>

11:30.120 --> 11:35.199
Look, Stewie, I gotta finish this assignment
or I'm gonna fail this class.

11:35.294 --> 11:38.711
- All done.
- What? I can't use this. It'd be cheating.

11:38.799 --> 11:44.093
Fine. I'll be out on the quad. You know what
I've discovered since I've been in college?

11:44.182 --> 11:47.435
I am so all about Ultimate Frisbee.

11:57.955 --> 12:00.826
<i>Oh, no! Did that hit Crazy Stairs?</i>

12:03.714 --> 12:05.589
I graded your assignments.

12:05.675 --> 12:12.132
Clearly there is only one person here
who understands the material - Brian Griffin.

12:13.479 --> 12:15.769
Just got lucky, I guess.

12:15.858 --> 12:19.027
No, Brian, I underestimated you.

12:19.114 --> 12:22.699
Here, let me put a smiley face on your test.

12:23.955 --> 12:26.494
May I borrow your pen?

12:26.584 --> 12:30.418
You... Do you...
Do you want me to just stick it in there?

12:30.507 --> 12:32.381
Yes.

12:40.189 --> 12:42.681
There. You have earned that.

12:52.082 --> 12:55.038
- Hey, what's up B-Ri?
- Stewie, just give me a beer.

12:55.129 --> 12:59.675
I've had a bad day.
I cheated on that assignment.

12:59.761 --> 13:04.391
You know, I haven't taken a shower since we
got here. I totally reek, man. Check this out.

13:04.477 --> 13:06.851
- Come on!
- Tell me that's not epic.

13:06.940 --> 13:11.271
I didn't come back to college to cheat
my way through. I wanted to do it on my own.

13:11.363 --> 13:13.605
Will you relax? Plenty of people cheat.

13:13.699 --> 13:16.192
Once again, Ashlee Simpson.

13:38.824 --> 13:42.905
Mom, look. They're tearing down
Roger Williams Park to build a strip mall.

13:42.996 --> 13:46.534
Oh, no, I take Stewie there all the time,
don't I, sweetie?

13:46.628 --> 13:48.705
Victory shall be mine.

13:48.798 --> 13:54.222
That's where I go to make out with
my boyfriend, Darren Mitchellstork.

13:54.306 --> 14:01.144
Yeah, he's the chairman
of the soccer ball team.

14:01.234 --> 14:07.073
Well, all right. Make sure
you practise safe sex, Meg.

14:09.831 --> 14:11.908
You little liar!

14:12.001 --> 14:16.380
Roger Williams Park?
That sounds like ajob for the A-Team.

14:18.720 --> 14:20.465
- Hi, Dad!
- Go to your room.

14:20.557 --> 14:22.431
OK.

14:30.030 --> 14:35.619
Ah, Brian, I am glad you could come
to my faculty cocktail party.

14:35.705 --> 14:38.328
Let me introduce my wife, Helen.

14:38.418 --> 14:42.963
Dammit, Steve, you forgot
to put out the cheese and crackers.

14:43.049 --> 14:47.002
Helen, don't start with me
in front of our guests.

14:49.352 --> 14:52.224
Do you think I like hitting you?

14:52.315 --> 14:54.986
I am sorry you had to see that.

14:55.069 --> 14:58.771
Look, sir, I need to confess something.
That assignment I turned in...

14:58.866 --> 15:00.826
You know, Brian,

15:00.912 --> 15:06.455
before you came along I was so depressed
I was planning to kill myself.

15:06.546 --> 15:08.540
But you have inspired me.

15:08.633 --> 15:12.882
If you can learn, maybe one day I can walk.

15:12.973 --> 15:15.679
Now, what was it you wanted to say?

15:15.769 --> 15:18.096
Nothing.

15:18.189 --> 15:22.105
You were supposed to get potato chips,
you jackass.

15:22.195 --> 15:28.238
Dammit, Helen, get the hell off my back
or so help me... so help me...

15:28.873 --> 15:31.912
Don't worry.
I hear they have great make-up sex.

15:32.003 --> 15:37.167
- Oh, that feels so good.
- Oh, oh, oh. Oh, yeah. Like that.

15:37.262 --> 15:40.964
- Oh, baby.
- I thought about this all day.

15:44.941 --> 15:48.940
Not so fast. You are hurting me.

15:53.787 --> 15:56.493
- All right.
- Stewie, come on, we're going home.

15:56.583 --> 15:59.540
- What are you talking about?
- My final exam is tomorrow.

15:59.631 --> 16:04.259
Only way I'll pass is if I cheat. If I do, what
was the point of coming back to college?

16:04.346 --> 16:09.473
We can't leave. It's almost half-time,
and we all pooped in the tuba.

16:11.817 --> 16:13.014
OK, we can go.

16:25.838 --> 16:28.509
Hey, what are you guys doing?
This is ajob site.

16:28.593 --> 16:33.638
No, it's not. It's Roger Williams Park and
we're here to stop you from destroying it.

16:33.726 --> 16:36.562
Whoa! What are you gonna do? Kill us?

16:36.646 --> 16:38.475
Oh, no, no. We wouldn't do that.

16:38.566 --> 16:42.103
We'll probably shoot the ground around you
to make you scared.

16:42.197 --> 16:45.866
Then you'll jump in your truck, speed off,
hit something and do a flip.

16:45.955 --> 16:49.704
- That'd kill us.
- No, you'll just roll out and dust yourself off

16:49.793 --> 16:51.870
and lumber to your hideout, defeated.

16:51.963 --> 16:55.250
I had a cousin got in a fender-bender
at five miles an hour.

16:55.344 --> 16:59.759
Messed his neck up, he's got partial
numbness, he's just not the same guy.

16:59.851 --> 17:02.259
- Was he wearing his safety belt?
- Thank God.

17:02.354 --> 17:05.606
Yeah, cos I know this guy
who took his car in for an oil change.

17:05.692 --> 17:08.481
Later he got in a wreck
and the air bag didn't deploy.

17:08.572 --> 17:11.860
- Turns out they stole it, sold it for spares.
- No way.

17:11.953 --> 17:15.904
It happens. They call 'em chop shops.
Makes it harder to track stolen parts.

17:16.001 --> 17:18.160
Jeez, that is awful.

17:18.254 --> 17:21.542
Well, you got a lot of work to do.
We should get out of your hair.

17:21.635 --> 17:23.712
- Take it easy, now.
- Yeah, see you.

17:23.805 --> 17:26.095
Be sure to put your tools away.

17:28.229 --> 17:31.018
- We blew it, didn't we?
- Boy, you can say that again.

17:31.109 --> 17:35.905
We were ready to save Roger Williams Park
and we got sidetracked by idle conversation.

17:35.991 --> 17:39.611
- We're a terrible A-Team.
- The problem is we didn't stay focused.

17:39.705 --> 17:44.085
That's exactly it. We didn't stay focused.
I mean, we were right there,

17:44.171 --> 17:48.386
and then we just...
Somehow we just... I mean... It...

17:48.469 --> 17:50.677
It's been said. We didn't stay focused.

17:52.267 --> 17:54.177
<i>Now back to The Facts of Life.</i>

17:54.270 --> 17:57.641
- Hey, Mrs Garrett, can I ask you something?
- What is it, Jo?

17:57.734 --> 18:00.654
Is it a problem
if your penis and your vagina touch?

18:00.739 --> 18:01.770
What?

18:01.866 --> 18:06.329
I try to keep 'em separated, but I woke up
this morning and they were sort of together.

18:06.415 --> 18:09.703
- I just didn't know. Is that OK?
- You have both?

18:09.796 --> 18:13.378
- Well, yeah, doesn't everybody?
- No!

18:13.466 --> 18:15.710
Brian, what are you doing home?

18:15.804 --> 18:19.091
I couldn't do it.
I thought I'd be able to finish this time,

18:19.184 --> 18:22.520
but I just don't have what it takes
to be a college graduate.

18:22.607 --> 18:26.357
But you're so close.
I mean, your final exam's tomorrow.

18:26.446 --> 18:30.114
You can't give up. You could study tonight.
I think if you work at it...

18:30.203 --> 18:33.656
Lois, Lois. It's over, all right?
I'm not going.

18:33.750 --> 18:36.242
Well, whatever you say.

18:36.337 --> 18:40.467
- Hey, what's in this closet?
- What are you doing?

18:40.551 --> 18:46.392
- Well, my my. Mr Hoover's come to visit.
- I don't wanna see Mr Hoover.

18:46.479 --> 18:49.352
I wonder if Mr Hoover has anything
to say about this.

18:49.441 --> 18:53.393
This is not funny.
I don't wanna see Mr Hoover.

18:53.865 --> 18:56.904
Stop! Stop it! Stop it! It's scaring me!

18:56.995 --> 18:59.950
Leave me alone! It's so loud!

19:00.041 --> 19:04.505
- Stop! Stop it! All right, OK, I'll study!
- I'll help you if you want.

19:04.590 --> 19:07.759
No thanks, Lois.
There's only one person who can help me.

19:36.850 --> 19:39.557
Drago!

19:43.568 --> 19:46.691
- The exam's in three hours.
- Crap. All we did was work out.

19:46.783 --> 19:48.158
- We should study.
- Right.

19:51.080 --> 19:53.407
You're not wearing your costume any more.

19:53.501 --> 19:57.287
What's the point? I thought I could
help people with this A-Team thing,

19:57.383 --> 20:02.380
<i>but it turns out I'm as useless as
that nude Playboy spread of Debbie Gibson.</i>

20:02.473 --> 20:05.227
It's like, "She's naked, but who gives a shit?"

20:05.312 --> 20:08.018
Oh, my God, I overslept.
My exam's in 20 minutes.

20:08.108 --> 20:10.232
Brian, you'll never make it.

20:10.320 --> 20:15.697
Unless there was some kind of team
of people who could get you there in time.

20:15.787 --> 20:18.576
Peter, do you know anybody like that?

20:29.475 --> 20:32.263
You may start your exam...

20:33.900 --> 20:35.857
now.

20:41.869 --> 20:44.279
- Well, how'd you do?
- I failed.

20:44.373 --> 20:46.201
- What? You failed?
- Yep.

20:46.293 --> 20:49.462
- What are you smiling for?
- Because I took it all the way.

20:49.548 --> 20:53.170
I didn't give up on myself, and I didn't cheat.

20:54.056 --> 20:56.595
- You probably should have.
- Yeah.

20:56.685 --> 20:59.806
- You would've been better off.
- What were you thinking?

20:59.898 --> 21:03.020
Doesn't matter how it turned out.
I finished what I started,

21:03.111 --> 21:06.482
which means I have my pride,
and that's something.

21:06.574 --> 21:09.115
- No, it's not.
- Are you out of your mind?

21:09.205 --> 21:11.412
- I don't understand.
- You're a loser.

21:11.500 --> 21:13.292
I hate you!

21:13.293 --> 22:14.293
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru